  "description": "Select optimal batch size maximizing token throughput while strictly respecting maximum latency SLO constraint.\n\nBatching increases GPU compute utilization and throughput at the expense of queuing and processing latency. SLO tuning finds the Pareto frontier.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\nB^* = \\arg\\max_{B} \\text{Throughput}(B) \\quad \\text{subject to} \\quad \\text{Latency}(B) \\le \\text{SLO}\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Filter candidate configurations satisfying latency <= max_latency_slo_ms\n2. Identify batch size delivering highest token throughput per second\n3. Return dictionary with optimal batch parameters\n\n### Returns\nDictionary with 'optimal_batch_size', 'latency_ms', and 'throughput'.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Optimize Throughput and Cost Under a Latency SLO\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nRunning large AI models in production requires massive computing power. During text generation, memory bandwidth (fetching weights and past key-value caches from VRAM) is often the primary bottleneck rather than raw arithmetic compute. **Optimize Throughput and Cost Under a Latency SLO** optimizes hardware efficiency, memory consumption, or request serving throughput.\n\nBatching increases GPU compute utilization and throughput at the expense of queuing and processing latency. SLO tuning finds the Pareto frontier. In this problem, the goal is to: select optimal batch size maximizing token throughput while strictly respecting maximum latency slo constraint.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\nB^* = \\arg\\max_{B} \\text{Throughput}(B) \\quad \\text{subject to} \\quad \\text{Latency}(B) \\le \\text{SLO}\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Filter candidate configurations satisfying latency <= max_latency_slo_ms\n2. **Phase 2**: Identify batch size delivering highest token throughput per second\n3. **Phase 3**: Return dictionary with optimal batch parameters\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Memory Bandwidth Bottleneck**: Quantizing weights to INT8 or INT4 cuts memory traffic in half or quarters, dramatically increasing token generation speeds.\n* **Serving Systems**: Dynamic batching and PagedAttention maximize GPU utilization by grouping requests arriving at different times.\n* **Latency vs. Throughput**: In production serving, systems engineers balance Time-To-First-Token (TTFT) against overall tokens-per-second throughput.",
  "examples": [
    "Input: batch_sizes = [1, 4, 16], latencies_ms = [20.0, 60.0, 150.0], throughputs_tok_per_sec = [50.0, 180.0, 400.0], max_latency_slo_ms = 100.0\n\nOutput: {\"optimal_batch_size\": 4, \"latency_ms\": 60.0, \"throughput\": 180.0}\n\nExplanation: Evaluated inference_throughput_cost_slo under standard test conditions."
